{"id":"03087ea1802e2ea2","group":"58","path":"58/batch05/58-df-sieve.md","title":"Sieve","display":"df-sieve — Sieve","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-sieve","aliases":["58-df-sieve","58-df-sieving","Sieve","Sieve Method","Eratosthenes Sieve"],"display":"df-sieve — Sieve","depends_on":["[[../batch19/58-df-prime-number.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-sieve"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-sieve</span><span>58-df-sieving</span><span>Sieve</span><span>Sieve Method</span><span>Eratosthenes Sieve</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-sieve — Sieve"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"dad686059f3ca152\" href=\"?note=dad686059f3ca152\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-prime-number.md\">../batch19/58-df-prime-number.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A,P,S\\in V\">\\(A,P,S\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Prime}:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Prime}:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"dad686059f3ca152\" href=\"?note=dad686059f3ca152\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-prime-number.md\">../batch19/58-df-prime-number.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SieveSet}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{SieveSet}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}sieve}\\vdash\\mathrm{SieveSet}_S(S,A,P)\\leftrightarrow A\\subseteq\\mathbb Z\\land P\\subseteq\\omega\\land\\forall p\\in P\\;\\mathrm{Prime}(p)\\land S=\\{a\\in A:\\forall p\\in P\\;(p\\nmid a)\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}sieve}\\vdash\\mathrm{SieveSet}_S(S,A,P)\\leftrightarrow A\\subseteq\\mathbb Z\\land P\\subseteq\\omega\\land\\forall p\\in P\\;\\mathrm{Prime}(p)\\land S=\\{a\\in A:\\forall p\\in P\\;(p\\nmid a)\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Sieve: eliminates numbers divisible by given primes; fundamental in prime counting</li>\n<li>The unique set <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S\">\\(S\\)</span> satisfying the predicate is conventionally denoted <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S(A,P)\">\\(S(A,P)\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>For bounds <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x,y\">\\(x,y\\)</span>, the same sifted set is written <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\{n\\leq x\\mid \\forall p\\leq y\\;(p\\nmid n)\\}\">\\(\\{n\\leq x\\mid \\forall p\\leq y\\;(p\\nmid n)\\}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Eratosthenes: classical sieve; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"O(N \\log \\log N)\">\\(O(N \\log \\log N)\\)</span>; remove multiples of primes <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\leq \\sqrt{N}\">\\(\\leq \\sqrt{N}\\)</span></li>\n<li>Selberg sieve: a weighted upper-bound sieve for sifted sets</li>\n<li>Large-sieve estimates control averaged arithmetic error terms and have applications to primes in progressions.</li>\n<li><code>58-df-sieving</code> is merged here; both files formalized sifted sets by removing multiples of primes.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Halberstam and Richert, Sieve Methods</li>\n<li>Iwaniec and Kowalski, Analytic Number Theory</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch19/58-df-prime-number.md","status":"resolved","id":"dad686059f3ca152","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch19/58-df-prime-number.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch19/58-df-prime-number.md","status":"resolved","id":"dad686059f3ca152","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Prime}:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}$ (see [[../batch19/58-df-prime-number.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"A,P,S\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Prime}:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SieveSet}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}sieve}\\vdash\\mathrm{SieveSet}_S(S,A,P)\\leftrightarrow A\\subseteq\\mathbb Z\\land P\\subseteq\\omega\\land\\forall p\\in P\\;\\mathrm{Prime}(p)\\land S=\\{a\\in A:\\forall p\\in P\\;(p\\nmid a)\\}","display":true},{"tex":"S","display":false},{"tex":"S(A,P)","display":false},{"tex":"x,y","display":false},{"tex":"\\{n\\leq x\\mid \\forall p\\leq y\\;(p\\nmid n)\\}","display":false},{"tex":"O(N \\log \\log N)","display":false},{"tex":"\\leq \\sqrt{N}","display":false}],"bytes":1409,"backlinks":[{"id":"8333e4d8ffbd048e","anchor":"ref-1","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"7b5e80183bd069e4","anchor":"ref-2","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1159","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch05/58-df-sieve.md|58-df-sieve]]（batch05）"}],"outgoing":["dad686059f3ca152"]}